{"id": "EUVD-2024-55773", "enisaUuid": "261a3c27-f35b-3489-b1f3-ac8eeb157b5a", "description": "A code injection vulnerability has been discovered in the Robot Operating System 2 (ROS 2) 'ros2topic' command-line tool, affecting all ROS 2 distributions from Crystal Clemmys up to and including Lyrical Luth and Rolling Ridley. The vulnerability lies in the 'hz' verb, which reports the publishing rate of a topic and accepts a user-provided Python expression via the --filter option. This input is passed directly to the eval() function without sanitization, allowing a local user to craft and execute arbitrary code.", "datePublished": "2026-09-28T21:38:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-30T13:43:15", "baseScore": 8.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ros2/ros2cli/pull/1001", "https://github.com/ros2/ros2cli/pull/133#discussion_r223081766"], "aliases": ["CVE-2024-42002"], "assigner": "canonical", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d773c52-b387-3351-b7d4-91569d5f87cc", "product": {"name": "Robot Operating System 2 (ROS 2)", "vendor": {"name": "Open Source Robotics Foundation"}}, "product_version": "Rolling Ridley"}, {"id": "1ec53130-96e0-38d5-9873-6e96e6d691e5", "product": {"name": "Robot Operating System 2 (ROS 2)", "vendor": {"name": "Open Source Robotics Foundation"}}, "product_version": "Humble Hawksbill"}, {"id": "37736ca4-6a41-3c90-9e6f-0f4c9906d41a", "product": {"name": "Robot Operating System 2 (ROS 2)", "vendor": {"name": "Open Source Robotics Foundation"}}, "product_version": "Foxy Fitzroy"}, {"id": "381df00a-1b66-3f91-85a9-2b19ec424015", "product": {"name": "Robot Operating System 2 (ROS 2)", "vendor": {"name": "Open Source Robotics Foundation"}}, "product_version": "Jazzy Jalisco"}, {"id": "5d556714-f15b-3d4d-827f-6f52fbc95062", "product": {"name": "Robot Operating System 2 (ROS 2)", "vendor": {"name": "Open Source Robotics Foundation"}}, "product_ve